Market Challenges
COS equipment must accommodate different plate configurations, battery dimensions and production requirements. Integrating new machinery into existing production lines can require engineering modifications, commissioning time and coordination with upstream and downstream equipment.

Market Restraints
High initial investment, specialized tooling requirements and maintenance complexity can affect purchasing decisions, particularly among smaller manufacturers. Lead handling, ventilation and workplace exposure controls also add to installation and operating costs. The gradual adoption of alternative battery technologies in selected applications may limit investment in some lead-acid production lines.

